  "contract": [
    "Authenticated weak slot0 Stringable SET conversion runs before old live INI lookup. A nonempty NUL-free result installs the value and returns the post-callback old value.",
    "Empty results return false; NUL raises ValueError. Both preserve callback-installed INI. Strict direct/first-class and non-Stringable operands reject before conversion; owned internal Closure->__invoke retains the weak boundary.",
    "INI_SET with an object second slot rejects before option lookup/mutation, without casting that value, using the native string|int|float|bool|null type message.",
    "CHDIR and SET kind/source guards remain disjoint. Shared child-name admission still requires authentic kind, source, line, object, contribution, ownership, selection and PACKS evidence."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only NUL-free old INI values are accepted here. Embedded-NUL C-prefix SET return and leading-NUL scalar ini_set behavior remain the original INI-option05 increment.",
    "Completed PACKS retain borrowed values without new roots; completed array IDs and integer-key numbers remain documentary.",
    "Restore04, INI-option05, CLI sentinel renderer, PIPE, real wrapper dispatch, broader OS/INI and lifecycle remain separate. No pending calls/property/compiler or paused returns changes are imported."
  ],
